            <ArticleTitle>Temporomandibular dysfunction, chronic orofacial pain and oral motor disorders in the 21st century.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>41-2, 44-6, 48-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article describes the various sensory and motor disorders that afflict the orofacial region. These abnormalities are broadly separated into three groups of pathologic conditions: temporomandibular disorders; chronic orofacial pain disorders; and oral motor disorders. This article focuses on the diagnostic features of each specific disorder, suggesting alternate nomenclature for each disorder.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
